fect our pay if we  say too many things to josh that make  him quest in his decision we'll get paid  less as the db wasn't as authentic but  if we avoid saying any of these options  we can get the most pay from it this  interaction at the end is incredibly  hard to watch as the nailing of his  wrist and legs is right in front of you  my original decision was to help nail  him to the cross as i believe that while  i didn't want him to go through with it  i should at least honor his dying wish  which was to be by his side for the  whole event by the way this quest does  not end until he dies so you must sit  and watch in real time as he slowly  loses consciousness this whole thing  lasts a full minute and is one of the  longest minutes of my life everything  about this quest was just so real there  were no gimmicks involved in this quest  and cd projekt red wanted there to be  none they wanted you to sit through the  entire process no matter how dark this  got the quest left the player with lots  of choices and this is truly a great  showcase of the writer's talent to  create a story that seems to have an  element of choice it's one quest that  has stuck with me for the past year and  one i probably won't ever forget  everything about this was just so  enthralling but terrifying i was  constantly waiting to see where this  quest would go but i was also worried  what would happen by the end the fact  that this quest has no characters  relevant to the main story and are only  seen during this quest just shows how  good this really is i never needed a  character from the main story or a plot  revolving around the main story to be  good it was just a stand-alone quest  with one of the best stories i've ever  seen our next quest is one that is also  deeply disturbing but in a different  context just like before we get a call  from a random person during our  playthrough this person is elizabeth  perales and she wants us to meet with  her and her husband jeff it sounds like