ns behind  reality tv probably my favorite was a  random guy on the end of a bridge he's  backed himself into a corner but has  managed to fend off all the police that  have arrived after subduing him you  discover from his laptop that he's a  combat veteran who suffers from severe  ptsd thankfully at his current job there  was a ptsd program that he could enroll  in but he was eventually fired and lost  that privilege leaving him no way to  handle his problems this caused him to  not keep a job causing him to be  homeless due to no income and eventually  led to how we see him in game there are  17 of these encounters in the game and i  can't think of a single one that was bad  each of them portrayed different people  from different walks of life and showed  how they got cyber psychosis and how  they're currently dealing with it it's  truly one of the best groups of side  content in the game which actually makes  me extremely upset as this is  overshadowed by all the other activities  that are some of the most boring content  i've played in a video game besides the  cyber psychos we have gigs and ncpd  hustles the gigs are a toss-up most of  them have the same content and depending  on your build might seem like the same  mission there are a few gigs that are  quite boring but do become very exciting  when you switch your playstyle like this  gig where i needed to take some guy from  this building and put him in the trunk  of a nearby car if i were to shoot the  place up i would just kill everyone then  carry the guy's body out but if i were  to play a sneak character then i would  try to avoid detection by sneaking my  way in like i said depending on your  play style some may feel unique but most  of the time it's the same content the  ncpd hustles however are just awful  there are a few different versions of  them all of which are basically the same  thing you complete the assaults and  progress by either killing all the  criminals and collecting the loot or  looting the crate undetected reported  crimes are beaten by killing all the  criminals in the area then grabbing the  illegally stashed loot an organized  crime is just killing all the criminals  in the area considering the fact that  the game's main gameplay loop is killing  enemies collecting their loot then  replacing your current gear with better  items it's just the same thing you've  been doing in any of the other missions  before this leads to all of these being  incredibly boring i can't recall a  single time i enjoy doing these and it  also showcases something quite unique  that there's no penalty for being caught  if there's an optional stealth objective  that you fail you might miss out on a  bit of rep or money but considering how  many of them there are in the game the  loss is negligible running and gunning  in this game is not only more exciting  but more efficient all you'll really be  doing is going to the location of the  hustle finishing it within two minutes  and then going to the next location  funny enough driving from one hustle to  the next is sometimes slower than doing  the actual hustle itself they're just  lazy and boring activities with a clear  lack of depth and interactivity that are  copy pasted so much it's hard to tell  what activity you're actually doing  speaking of which another example of  poor depth and development is the gangs  and fixers in cyberpunk the gangs and  fixers in this game are incredibly  shallow every district in the city has a  head fixer and a gang that holds the  territory the gangs only exist to be  shot at and the fixers really shouldn't  even be on the map at all all the gang's  backstories and values are incredibly  unique maelstrom is a psycho gang  dedicated to putting in as many implants  as possible and the animals prefer to  use their cyberware to increase their  strength i also believe they're the only  gang in the game that will attack the  player with just their fist the story of  these gangs is incredible but everything  else in game is awful because there is  nothing else on rare occasions you can  work with certain gangs like the voodoo  boys or maelstrom assuming you pick the  correct choices but that's just in one  mission some of the gangs like sixth  street and the tiger claws do absolutely  nothing with the players so they are  literally just made to be shot at there  is no way to be recruited into these  gangs or even ask them for assistance it  feels like such a waste of potential as  these games could have had a much larger  role in the game but they were just put  to be target dummies the fixers fall  into the same problem the only thing the  fixers do is call you about missions and  call you about cars them calling about  cars just feels so far off from what  they actually do in the game i feel like  cd projekt red needed some way to give  the player new vehicles so instead of  just adding car dealers they just gave  them to the fixers and it's not even  that engaging either the fixer just  randomly sends you a text of a car  nearby to which a map marker of its  location permanently stays on your map  to buy the car you just go over and hop  in and the game will take your money i'm  pretty sure all these vehicles just  exist on the map you can't steal them  from people or rob the keys from the  owner they're just cars that exist the  missions are just as bad the fixtures  will call and text you about mission  details seeing as most of these missions  are pretty much the same thing minus a  few instances there's really no point to  read the details since you already know  what to do you either kill or sneak your  way into this building than either grab  the loot rescue the person retrieve the  car etc this is all the fixers have been  reduced to you can visit them on the map  but you're only given two to three  dialogue options and that's all  something as small as giving them a  personal mission would have been great  not something from a client but 