tances crit damage and  explosions this is where your initial  build will start however you can go  deeper from here you could go fully into  firearms and use the body stat for  health and defense then level up the  reflexes stat to get more damage skills  but if you prefer sneaking you could  replace the body stat with cool and have  a silent range build there's definitely  a lot of potential with these builds and  they can be very fun to try out and use  the game even lets you respect your  skills if you want to move things around  except it's only the skills not the  attributes so you're still stuck in the  same archetype you created but are  allowed to change the my new details of  your skill set i personally wish this  was able to be respect but the only  reason i can think of as to why is that  they didn't add this part because people  could just respect their skills if they  lack the attribute level to bypass a  door or something not only does this  sound incredibly tedious it's also the  same thing with save scumming yes being  able to save any time and anywhere does  promote safe scumming but the positives  outweigh the negatives greatly besides  the standard weaponry you can find on  enemies or in crates you can also equip  yourself with cyberware that can greatly  enhance any build you want to play with  loud and proud players can even replace  their operating system with cyberware  that doesn't even have any ram slots or  quick hacks seeing as you won't be using  them in the first place this now allows  you to gain buffs from other equipment  as for what we have cyberpunk definitely  tries its best to make combat fun by  giving the player numerous trees to pick  from allowing for tons of different  builds every playthrough however for me  i wasn't always having that much fun  with its combat i recognize this is  totally subjective as lots of people  have different tastes some people prefer  to use stealth whenever possible when i  try to never use it unless i have to so  already there's going to be some bias  towards certain archetypes so as for  stealth i will say that it was quite fun  despite me preferring a different  playstyle stealth with the introduction  of quick hacking can really change this  game in a drastic way because not only  could you never engage in combat you'll  never be close to anyone either quick  hacks will go as far as your scanner  goes and depending on your operating  system and abilities you may never even  need a weapon i do highly recommend  playing this way if you enjoy stealth as  it was really fun when things went right  blades were by far my favorite weapon to  use as with the right skills not a  single enemy is challenging the blades  are also one section of the skill tree  so once you maximize a good portion of  the stats you need you can just put  those extra points and dump them into  other stats like increased armor or  health allowing you to be pretty much  unkillable the blades were always a  blast to use however the gun play felt a  little dull there was such a large  selection of different guns that it's  quite easy to gravitate towards a  favorite weapon some of these weapons  even have special traits like smart  rounds and ricocheting bullets but due  to the game's ammo system in combination  with its skills it severely limits your  options smg's lmgs precision rifles and  ars all share the same ammo type and all  of these but lmgs are in the same skill  tree so you can have an assault rifle  smg and lmg under character you're just  going to waste all your ammo since the  game gives us three weapons to use we  need to fill those other roles which are  either shotguns pistols snipers or even  melee if we wanted to dabble into it but  due to how the skill trees are separated  you'll more than likely have three guns  with mediocre upgrades or one gun with  incredible upgrades and the other two  with next to nothing and while it's not  the end-all be-all of this game the  upgrades are very important as they do  make your weapons stronger this also  becomes more of a problem later when you  have to change weapons the same weapon  you're currently using could be swapped  for the same one since the enemy that  died was higher than you thus making  that gun automatically better while this  example is not as bad it becomes a  problem when you have to swap a weapon  that you didn't want to use but now need  to use because its stats are just better  this also goes for your armor as well  this game is one where you need to  prioritize your stats or your fashion as  there's no way to change the look of the  armor and keep its stats the very last  part of its gameplay though is its  crafting and to be completely honest  with you i've never touched crafting in  this game i find it extremely  unnecessary crafting is nice if you want  to make more grenades health inhalers or  even make upgraded versions of legendary  gear but i never needed to most of my  armor and weapons were getting  outclassed as i ranked up so there was  no point in spending all this time and  money on upgrade components when they  would just get outmatched by any weapon  to add to this i also never ran out of  inhalers or grenades i could definitely  see some use out of it on higher  difficulties when you need a specific  health booster to heal but i just never  ran out assuming you loot enough of the  bodies in each area you'll have more  than enough gear to go around that  crafting was just an afterthought to me  cyberpunk's gameplay variety is very fun  and does allow for lots of creativity  when it comes to builds you want it  allows for endless possibilities and  that is a very important feature for a  game like this but while its blades and  stealth were fun the gun play in the  game just felt a bit confusing as it  seems to encourage using a diverse  arsenal of weapons but it also hinders  the potential of said weapons by making  the ammo the same for most of its guns 