a's mom who's not as happy as  zuleika is to see josh in her home again  she kicks both of us out and then we  head to a nearby restaurant for some  quick food this ends the quest for now  until we get a call a couple days later  where we can continue this was such a  fantastic idea for the quest and the  amount of options we are given is  incredible after our visit with zuleika  rachel will pull us aside and talk about  josh she mentions how he's very valuable  to the company and it's because of his  authenticity he's not putting on some  act for the braindance he genuinely  believes his crucifixion can change the  world it's because of this that prompts  rachel to bring us aside where she tells  us to leave if we keep talking to josh  we might screw up the job and get him to  question his decision so she's trying to  avoid that entirely by paying us double  the original amount if we leave this  section also brings up a good point and  it's that this mission gives us numerous  times to just leave and drop the quest  i'm unsure if it's because of the heavy  subject matter within the quest but we  can leave five different times  throughout these missions one is before  we get in the van another while we are  in the van and learn about him in his  heavenly journey the third after we  discover the truth about his crucifixion  the fourth being here with rachel and  the fifth one during the last mission  it's nice that the game is letting the  player leave if things get too heavy  it's a nice way of not forcing the  player to do something they might not  want to do going back to the mission the  reason there is another quest is because  josh is second guessing his decisions  here's where we can do one of many  things no matter what happens josh will  be crucified but we can either help nail  him to the cross not help him but watch  or just leave this choice and other  dialogue choices throughout the missions  will affect the overall quality of the  db and in turn also affect our pay if we  say too many things to josh that make  him quest in his decision we'll get paid  less as the db wasn't as authentic but  if we avoid saying any of these options  we can get the most pay from it this  interaction at the end is incredibly  hard to watch as the nailing of his  wrist and legs is right in front of you  my original decision was to help nail  him to the cross as i believe that while  i didn't want him to go through with it  i should at least honor his dying wish  which was to be by his side for the  whole event by the way this quest does  not end until he dies so you must sit  and watch in real time as he slowly  loses consciousness this whole thing  lasts a full minute and is one of the  longest minutes of my life everything  about this quest was just so real there  were no gimmicks involved in this quest  and cd projekt red wanted there to be  none they wanted you to sit through the  entire process no matter how dark this  got the quest left the player with lots  of choices and this is truly a great  showcase of the writer's talent to  create a story that seems to have an  element of choice it's one quest that  has stuck with me for the past year and  one i probably won't ever forget  everything about this was just so  enthralling but terrifying i was  constantly waiting to see where this  quest would go but i was also worried  what would happen by the end the fact  that this quest has no characters  relevant to the main story and are only  seen during this quest just shows how  good this really is i never needed a  character from the main story or a plot  revolving around the main story to be  good it was just a stand-alone quest  with one of the best stories i've ever  seen our next quest is one that is also  deeply disturbing but in a different  context just like before we get a call  from a random person during our  playthrough this person is elizabeth  perales and she wants us to meet with  her and her husband jeff it sounds like