to help her  on the farm and since anthony was a kid  at the time he obviously didn't know too  much about farming so he was bound to  make mistakes and whenever he did his  father would ridicule him for it he also  had so much pent-up anger from his dad  that he even lashed out and killed his  mom shortly after this the father's  business would fail and due to this  failure he would kill himself so now  anthony was an orphan with seemingly no  friends or support system to manage his  problems the only thing that kept him  calm was that cartoon of the farmer  earlier he became so fascinated with the  farm and that cartoon that he continued  his dad's work of running the farm but  instead of using cows he used people  they were all hooked up to these giant  machines that pumped various chemicals  and gases into their lungs through the  brain dance we managed to discover where  the farm is and after breaking inside we  can rescue randy and all the others that  managed to survive this just like the  quest with josh was such a memorable  experience it was a shocking and  horrifying investigation where the  outcome was never certain it was never  clear if randy was actually going to  survive or not and that added some  urgency and tension to this quest  something i discovered recently was that  you can actually fail this quest if you  don't get enough evidence during the  brain dance we have to choose between  two farms and if you choose the wrong  one then randy dies i'm honestly  surprised this was an option but this  just adds another layer of urgency as  randy could actually die if we choose  wrong detective quests in many games are  always really intriguing especially when  they play into the world of the game and  with a game like cyberpunk where the  world is technologically advanced  anything can happen and i think that's a  big reason why this was so fun we truly  didn't know how the cyberware and  technology of night city would have a  hand in this quest structure and the way  it was utilized was really impressive  while river's questline was shorter than  most of the multi-stage quests in this  game it has by far one of the most  memorable moments due to its disturbing  content our last quest is once again  related to the previous interaction but  this time we'll talk about the other  side of it jefferson perales holds the  title for the greatest side quest in the  entire game it is not only a fantastic  quest with an incredible story but it is  so compelling that judging from the  comments on my previous video about it  many people wanted this developed into a  full dlc the quest line originally is  quite average and seems to exist just so  that the player can be introduced to  river however a couple days after  completing the original quest you'll  receive another message from jeff's wife  elizabeth the couple had a break-in and  they want to know who and why seeing as  jeff is in the running for mayor there's  a lot this investigation could bring up  as is possible that someone is targeting  him because he's rich or the person he's  running against is trying to eliminate  him the two of them want us to look into  it since we already unraveled the  mystery of the mayor's death plus they  already tried their private security  firm and they came up with nothing the  only details we can get from jeff is  that someone ended up breaking in when  he noticed he reached for his gun and  possibly shot the intruder before  passing out and waking up the next  morning with a terrible headache this  quest provides the player with an  immense amount of freedom as while  elizabeth does show you the penthouse  you can get a lay of the land she never  explicitly tells you what to search for  it's all on you to find the clues  furthermore some clues like this screen  can't be turned on unless you spec in a  technical ability and some doors won't  open without enough points in the body  tree obviously the game isn't going to  make the players spec into a specific  tree to complete the quest as that would  be quite frustrating but they do give  the players more optional clues if the  player has the proper skills everything  we investigate also comes with a bit of  dialogue that not only gives us more  hints about the investigation but also  further develops the couple as  characters by investigating the table  elizabeth will tell us about the  election process like how they're paying  for everything out of pocket and because  of how much work there is to do they  just order pizza most days as is too  hard to cook it's just genuine fantastic  storytelling as it's making the powerful  rich people seem like common folk but  also making these fictional characters  seem real and fully developed we  eventually begin to uncover the story of  the break-in as we see some emails from  the private security firm jeff had hired  and in one of these emails is a code to  a room this is already quite suspicious  since the room is only accessible via a  hidden door that the couple had no idea  existed however continuing on we  understand the full story once we read  the other emails that talk about one of  its members being shot by target alpha  this explains the bandages inside the  room but this also connects the entire  story that jeff is target alpha and the  security firm has been spying on them  the entire time after some further  investigation we noticed a satellite  dish on the roof and a comms tower  implying that the security team is  nearby we chase down the van and after  killing all the enemies we try to get  the data from the van until it's wiped  by an external source from what we saw  though it seems like they have brain  scan data on the couple and are using  neural links to implant new memories  into them this connects to one of the  clues we discovered earlier which is the  couple's wedding photo when  investigating this photo elizabeth will  say that she ordered blue roses for the  wedding despite the picture clearly  having red roses the last thing we get  to see before were shot out of the van  is that other people have been infected  with new memories too these people  aren't important but it's showing us  that jeff isn't a unique case they're  doing this to anybody regardless of  gender ethnicity or income we relay the  information to elizabeth who offers to  discuss the matter in private the game  isn't done with twists as we discovered  that elizabeth knew about these changes  in jeff his personality had changed  overnight and it almost felt like he was  a completely different person elizabeth  even noticed herself changing and once  it started getting worse she was in such  a total state of panic that she didn't  even know if she could trust her own  judgment she also got a call from  someone in a garbled voice telling her  that her family's safety and happiness  could end real soon if she attempts to  figure out the truth this presents the  player with an interesting dilemma as we  have the option to tell jefferson about  this discovery if we tell him we could  possibly ruin the lives of the couple  but it allows jeff to know the truth or  we can keep it a secret and never tell  him it's got its own set of moral  choices as some may argue that the  safety of the family is more important  but some could also argue that jeff has  a right to know what's going on however  what's more important is what happens in  the quest this quest was the start of a  massive community theory based around a  group called alpha centauri it's quite a  complex theory so if you want to know  everything you can check out my video on  it but to give you the short version  there was something very sinister  happening in this game that could  possibly affect all the citizens within  its walls if they get their way when we  approach jeff during the final part of  the quest we short circuit temporarily  as a garbled voice talks to us it's  quite possible that this was the same  garbled voice that elizabeth heard on  top of this nearby watching over our  discussion is mr blue eyes the same one  from the rogue ending he's not here  before the meeting and he leaves the  moment we're finished so that pretty  much confirms that he's only here  because of our discussion with jeff the  theory doesn't stop here as we have even  more clues as at some random point in  the game we get a call from sandra  dorsett which is the girl we saved from  the intro she needs our help getting  back a data bank that was stolen from  her if we go against her wishes and read  the shard we see that this operation  carpe noctum is eerily similar to what's  going on with the paralyzes furthermore  mr blue eyes also has this very unique  ring on his finger it's also very  similar to the ones worn by big joe  arthur jenkins jeff perales gary the  prophet and anders hellman they're all  slightly different in color in design  which may imply that they're either  marked by the organization behind the  brain scans or employed by them in some  way it's possible that mr blue eyes is  trying to further this organization's  agenda by having v attack the crystal  palace which we see in the ending this  is why this whole theory is so  compelling because most of these  characters are relevant to some of the  game's endings so it leaves this  open-ended question about what's really  going on it's without a doubt the best  side quest in the entire game and by far  one of the best waves i've seen a theory  be developed as it serves as a blueprint  for how an engaging quest should be one  thing you may have noticed is that all  the quests that i brought up today have  the story at the forefront there was  little to no combat in any of these  quests and i hope the reception and  positivity these quests received from  the community tells cd projekt red they  don't have to base the entire game  around combat not everything is about  shooting people and collecting loot  that's why the side activities were so  boring as it all felt repetitive but  with these i never felt bored and in  fact i was more engaged in the game than  ever obviously not every quest is like  this and many of them still have lots of  combat involved in them but regardless  of combat or not a majority of cyberpunk  side quests are well written and  incredibly captivating they're without a  doubt cyberpunk's biggest strength and i  hope they continue to lean heavily into  this content in a future dlc  keeping with the theme of positivity  let's end the video on a high note and  talk about its story i think this story  is fantastic is it the best narrative  i've ever seen absolutely not but just  by playing this game you can tell that  there's lots of passion put into it  furthermore the themes within the game  are quite thought-provoking and if a  game can make me think about its story  even after finishing it then it  succeeded cyberpunk is a story about the  race to immortality other ritual  continued reign over the poor forever  but it's also a story about one specific  murk who wants to make it to the top  however due to certain choices and  actions throughout their journey that  dream of theirs will come crashing down  the game is split into three acts act  one is before meeting johnny act three  is the ending and act two is everything  in between act one on a first  playthrough is really exciting it's the  beginning of a new game so you're  eagerly waiting for what comes next  after completing the life path we get a  six month time lapse of v and jackie's  life until we're given control again and  are about to start a job i have an  obvious issue with that time lapse that  many of you will agree with but i'll get  back to that later the first job is  quite basic and is more to get you  familiar with all the game's mechanics  after this mission is where things start  to evolve as we are notified that the  police are shutting down the watson  district the game locks us out of the  other districts until the first act is  over but it still gives us all the  content within the district so it's a  nice way to ease the player into the  game's side activities but not overwhelm  them by unlocking everything we're still  not done with the tutorials as we're  introduced to the ripper doc clinics and  then are given a quest with a great deal  of choices cd projekt red did an  incredible job making the first act as i  was able to see everything the game had  to offer but was also only allowed to go  within the first district so that i  never felt lost trying to explore the  whole map that mission i previously  mentioned is quite impressive and gives  the player lots of freedom the main goal  of the mission is to obtain this  flathead bot from the gang maelstrom  dexter deshawn the one who gives us the  job has already paid for it but never  got the bot and is hoping we can handle  that issue while maelstrom seems like  the only people involved in the quest  there's also a woman named meredith  stout who's involved there is an  optional objective to call and meet with  her which can potentially lead to a deal  the other person with her is andrew  gilchrist who is also important so now  we have three different people that can  be affected by our choices all the  options lead into two main branches we  can either resolve things peacefully  with maelstrom or slaughter everyone in  the building then because of this choice  and other choices i'll get to shortly  we'll either involve gilchrist or stout  meeting us at the entrance firstly when  we meet with maelstrom we can pay for  the flathead in a few ways either buying  it with our own money a credit chip that  style gave to us or just shooting  maelstrom and taking it ourselves this  credit chip leads to other options as  the chip that style gave us was infected  we can either leave the virus which will  make us hostile to maelstrom or if we  wipe out the virus then tell brick about  it we can work with him to defeat  militech pretty much any option that  forces us to shoot militech ends with  gilchrist at the end of the quest and  any option that makes maelstrom our  target will have stout at the end of the  quest these are just about every option  involved in this quest and it really  allows for that feeling of freedom you  have so many options and so many options  within options that it's overwhelming to  piece all them together it's just  upsetting that as we continue most of  the game it's quite linear from here  after doing all the tasks that dexter  has assigned us he meets with us to  discuss the real reason we did all this  prep work at a building called kampeki  plaza there is a penthouse owned by yori  nobu arasaka the son of saburo arasaka  apparently in this room there is a  device called the biochip and is  extremely expensive our client evelyn  parker who we met previously wants this  biochip this is where we get introduced  to the brain dances of cyberpunk end  once again more on those in a moment  jackie and v's job is to infiltrate the  building sneak into yori noble's room  and steal the chip everything goes  completely backwards as yorinubu comes  back to his room and has a meeting with  saburo it continues to go even further  south as he strangles his own father and  puts the building in lockdown the two  used the opportunity to escape until  their escape attempt ruined the case the  biochip was in and it needs to be put  into someone's head for it to maintain  the temperature despite both of them  being injured they managed to make it  downstairs and escape the plaza until  jackie succumbs to his wounds and dies  so  where to begin firstly this act was a  roller coaster of emotions in a good way  it was a really well made first act  although one of my biggest complaints is  this axe length even on repeat  playthroughs assuming you skipped  through all the dialogue this will take  about 2 hours i don't consider the game  to start until act 2 is that's when  everything is open and available to the  player without any restriction this act  is actually what stops me from playing  the game sometimes since i know i need  to get through this incredibly long act  before i can actually explore night city  what definitely doesn't help is that  long brain dance introduction too on  your first playthrough the braindances  were great but now knowing i have to go  through them again on another  playthrough is just exhausting this is  what makes this act so hard to talk  about running through this on your first  playthrough is wonderful and i have no  issues with it but on future  playthroughs it starts to become really  tedious while this does bother me it is  really situational as not everyone will  feel the same about the first act as i  do and some people may not even play the  game for another playthrough regardless  what's more important is jackie i've  come to the conclusion that cd projekt  red did not care about jackie as they  wanted the player to focus more on  johnny than they did jackie which is  quite ironic considering more people  like jackie the reason i say this is  because of the time lapse from earlier  and his death the less time we spend  with jackie the less opportunities we  have to build a relationship with him i  would have much rather preferred the  game just make me do these missions with  jackie rather than just showing us a  time lapse because i stopped caring we  aren't building that connection together  through our jobs and we're not feeling  like an actual team we aren't helping  one another during combat engagements or  just working together the intro is a  really good example is you and jackie  can work together to defeat the guy with  the machine gun by being a distraction  while jackie tackles him you feel like a  fully functioning team that is working  together to achieve a goal everything  else you do with him doesn't feel like  this the only times we join him are when  we buy the flathead and when we steal  the biochip but everything is done by  yourself you control the decisions of  the maelstrom conflict and you control  the flathead so you're able to get  inside yorinobu's room he just feels  like a companion that tags along and  will do what you do and go where you go  he isn't given an opportunity to shine  on his own his death also bothers me  greatly because this had zero impact on  me i sound like a heartless person but  it's not because i had no attachment to  jackie it's because cd projekt red  spoiled this in a trailer a year before  the game's launch in their e3 2019  trailer jackie and v escape a building  and use the delamane taxi service to  drive away then jackie shortly dies  after just like in game this trailer  shows us jackie and says his name which  means this person who may or may not be  in the game is jackie they didn't even  try to hide his haircut or face as he  looks exactly like the way he does in  game so prepare for the game i watched  most of the trailers again like the 48  minute gameplay demo and this cinematic  trailer because i thought it looked  really nice so imagine my face when i  found out that this jackie person is in  fact a real character in the game there  was still some hope in my mind that we  could maybe save him or he wouldn't have  been shot at all but that started coming  true when i noticed him limping with a  bullet wound in his stomach if you're  going to make me care about a character  don't show them dying in a trailer prior  to the game's release if jackie's death  managed to surprise you then i'm glad as  the way this was shown to the player and  how the next interaction starts with  that slow faded intro and low monotone  voice of v was really well done but it  was completely ruined for me as i saw it  coming way earlier than i should have  before we enter act 2 we see v approach  the note motel to meet dex who then  shoots him for screwing up the job we  then finally get introduced to johnny  silverhand and get to see how the  arasaka tower was destroyed 50 years ago  it's a nice introduction it really  highlights how much of a [ __ ] johnny  can be as instead of just dropping the  bomb and leaving he needed to complete  another personal mission of his which is  how he got killed this is where the big  plot twist of the game starts as it's  discovered that v will die within a few  weeks before jackie died he took the  biochip out of his head and gave it to v  when dex killed v the nanites and the  biochip were working on repairing his  brain but since he wasn't fully brain  dead yet the nanites could only repair  part of his brain which is why johnny  and v can co-exist the problem is that  this isn't supposed to happen is either  v or johnny not both which is why v is  slowly dying as the biochip is eating  away at his central nervous system these  main goal now has changed as instead of  making it to the top he's now  desperately trying to save his own life  this was a really nice plot change and a  nice way of putting it into perspective  of how the fear of immortality can  change you can you imagine how it must  feel to hear someone say you have weeks  to live when the day prior your death  wasn't even on your mind and you'd  figured you just die of old age all  those things you wanted to accomplish or  do in life won't ever be finished as  your life expectancy has been  drastically reduced in the blink of an  eye cd projekt red really wanted to  capture the desperation and fear of  something like this and i think they  nailed it act 2 starts and ends really  strong as we get introduced to johnny  silverhand it's very apparent from the  very first conversation they have that  the two are bitter enemies and want  nothing to do with one another v wants  johnny out so that he can live and  johnny wants to take over control of v  so that he can get revenge on arasaka  again the game allows you to play into  this as you can cut conversations with  him short by taking your prescribed  pills or just outright leaving it was  nice that the devs had given you the  option to truly express how you feel  about johnny through gameplay however i  don't think johnny is a bad person  kinda yes he's still an [ __ ] who  killed a ton of innocent people and his  ego never really goes away throughout  the game but at least between him and v  things do change between the two johnny  gets more sentimental and calm in the  later parts of the game and he comes to  accept the fact that he can't change the  world and he's just a ghost in v's head  v is also dealing with this frustration  as the entirety of act 2 is about  searching for a cure he tries to find  evelyn to see if she has any info on the  chip and this doesn't work but thanks to  some braindance v ends up working with  the voodoo boys but that didn't work  either he even captures the creator of  the chip and not even he can help him  these failures aren't just affecting v  it's affecting us too we're like  detectives trying to find new leads but  every single one we find leads to a dead  end and we're running out of options the  two of them are struggling together and  eventually learn to accept the other and  are willing to help one another to  complete their goal the two by the end  of the game have seemingly exhausted  every option possible except one as the  only one that has shown any promise is  hanako arasaka the sister of yorinobu  thanks to her interrogation with helman  v is able to download the blueprints of  the biochip and uses this data to strike  a deal with hanukkah the start of act 2  sees v being rescued by takamura the  same one who guards saburo arasaka  takamura is the only one who believes  that yuri nobu murdered saburo sakamura  is also on the run as yuri nobu betrayed  him so he wants to get back at your  renobu and find justice for saburo so  takamura works with v to discuss each  other's plans and eventually agree to  meet with hanako takamura wants to meet  with her to prove that yorinobu is a  killer envy wants to meet with her to  see if she can get him access to a place  called mikoshi mikoshi is the only  reason that johnny is alive and in our  head after blowing up arasaka tower they  stored his soul on a data drive and kept  it in this place called mikoshi this  place holds other people who signed up  for the secure your soul program  originally it was used for people to  talk to the dead after they had already  passed but there was a newer version of  this tech made and it's the one that's  in our head instead of someone being a  hologram after death they can take over  a person's body so they can continue to  live just be in the body of another  person this would then allow that person  to be immortal v needs to use mikoshi's  access point so that he can split  himself and johnny so that he doesn't  die v then discovers that mikoshi is  deep in arasaka tower so we know where  to go but we don't know how to get  inside the game then provides us with  four ways to accomplish this and are  considered the game's four endings our  first option is v working with hanako so  that they can bring down yorinobu  arasaka and bring sabro back into power  once again after this happens its top  scientists will help v with the chip  instead of that route we can either have  pam and the aldo caldos join us and  break into the tower or have johnny take  over our body and instead of those two  it's now rogue and wayland if none of  these satisfy the player they can always  take the easy route and commit suicide  the player is given many choices and the  way they set the scene was brilliant as  it's just you on a rooftop looking at  night city trying to make your final  decision the game lets you sit here as  long as you need so you never need to  feel rushed about your final choice cd  projekt red wants you to consider  everything you've gone through and  everything you felt throughout the game  and use those emotions and feelings to  make a decision each ending invokes  something throughout its time and it  gets the player thinking about their  decision what really hits the hardest is  the moment when you discover that every  ending ends in your death the biochip  has progressed so far that survival is  not possible anymore it invoked a  feeling in me that i haven't experienced  in many games that feeling being that  everything i did was completely useless  we were doomed from the beginning and it  was all for nothing that's what makes  these endings so great and this decision  has an impact on other people's lives  not just your own if you join arasaka  then we discovered that they used you as  a test on me and were able to replicate  the process allowing saburo to live in  yorinobu's body zeburo is no longer  bound by the body and can simply take  over a new one when the current one he's  using has passed in our desperate  attempt to help ourselves we let the  biggest corporation in the world learn  the secret to immortality if we do the  suicide ending then we affect everyone  that we've ever met it's the easy way  out and the least bloody option but  what's the point of going through all  this work just to give up at the very  end the final two decisions are not just  about johnny and v's relationship but  our relationship with johnny v is  destined to die within six months so we  either keep our body and say goodbye to  johnny or have johnny take our body  instead according to all tv's own body  sees him as an intruder now and we are  left with a decision let v keep the body  and live out his life for the next few  months until he dies or give it to  johnny who can live much longer and also  be able to experience a new life again  not bound by his rocker boy persona it's  a tough decision of sacrificing your  life for a friend or continue to live  but also having to say goodbye to yet  another friend cyberpunk's ending was  fantastic and while it was very sad that  nothing we did truly mattered in the end  the way the story was told was extremely  well done as for my final thoughts on  the game  cyberpunk is always going to be a  phenomenon of the gaming industry never  have i seen a game gather so much hype  and also simultaneously let everyone  down at the same time as i said before  cyberpunk isn't a good game but it's  also not a bad game either its gangs and  fixers feel underdeveloped its technical  issues are still very prevalent today  and some of its systems like crafting  inside activities are just boring dull  and useless however if you want to play  the game for its story then you will not  be sorry its attention to detail within  its open world makes it one of the most  gorgeous settings i've stepped foot in  and its side quest and story are worth  buying the game for just that alone  cyberpunk to me has always been a  complicated game to discuss because it  wasn't overwhelmingly good or bad to me  it was just perfectly average but with  some time and hope this game could maybe  become what it was originally intended  to be  thank you all for watching today's video  if you enjoyed then leave a like and  consider subscribing for more content  like this if you want to check out a  video similar in style to this then i  recommend my full analysis on the halo  series or prey both are quite long but  if you've made it this far in the video  that shouldn't matter and you don't need  to watch those videos in one sitting of  course you can always watch all the lore  videos i made back then on cyberpunk as  some of the content discussed in this  video had full videos dedicated to it  like the side quests and cyber psychosis  regardless thank you for making it to  the end and to my returning viewers i  thank you for coming back  take care everyone  goodbye  [Music]  so  [Music]
 

